# Cloudflare Pages cache rules.
#
# Pages already sends `Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` plus an
# ETag on every static asset, which its docs describe as guaranteeing that stale
# content is never served: the browser keeps its copy and revalidates, so an
# unchanged file costs a 304 rather than a re-download. That default is correct
# for this site, and the rule below states it rather than changing it, so the
# behaviour survives a change of host or of Cloudflare's defaults.
#
# The default is /* and not /*.html because Pages serves extensionless URLs: the
# page people visit is /events, which a /*.html rule never matches.
#
# Deliberately NO long cache on images or video. An earlier version of this file
# gave assets/img and assets/video a year, on the assumption that changed media
# would get a new filename. Nothing enforces that, and in practice clips are
# re-encoded in place under the same name — bar-night.webm was replaced three
# times in one afternoon. Under a year-long cache a returning visitor would keep
# the first version they ever loaded. Revalidation costs a 304; being wrong
# costs a visitor seeing last season's menu.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Fonts are the one safe exception: a given file's bytes never change, because a
# different weight or family means a different filename.
/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
